1. What you may do

   You may view this repository on GitHub, and fork it on GitHub solely to
   prepare and submit pull requests to this repository.

2. What you may not do

   Without prior written permission from the maintainers, you may not, in whole
   or in part, for commercial or non-commercial purposes:

   a. copy, download in bulk, scrape, mirror or archive the data;
   b. publish, redistribute, sell, sublicense or otherwise make it available;
   c. use it in, or to build, any website, app, API, product, service or
      dataset;
   d. use it to train, fine-tune, evaluate or ground any machine learning or
      AI model or system.

3. Contributions

   By submitting a pull request, issue or other contribution, you confirm that
   you have the right to submit it, and you grant the maintainers a perpetual,
   worldwide, irrevocable, royalty-free, non-exclusive license to use, copy,
   modify, publish, sublicense and distribute your contribution, as part of
   this repository and in any product built from it. You keep any rights you
   have in your contribution.

4. Third-party names

   Conference names, logos and trademarks belong to their owners. Their
   appearance here does not imply endorsement.

5. Removal requests

   If you are a speaker or organizer and want information about you removed,
   open an issue in this repository.

6. No warranty

   The data is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The maintainers
   are not liable for any claim or damages arising from it.

7. Third-party data

   Some rows were imported from third-party datasets and are marked with a
   "source" field. Those rows keep the terms of their source, which this
   LICENSE does not replace or restrict. Rows marked "confs.tech" come from
   https://github.com/tech-conferences/conference-data under the MIT License;
   see the Credits section of README.md.

To ask for permission to use the data, open an issue in this repository.
